# Custom App Setup

When **creating a new custom app** or **bootstrapping tooling on an existing app**, follow
[custom_app_setup.md](../project_base_template/custom_app_setup.md) exactly.

Do **not** invent alternate configs. Copy templates from that file (replace
`<app_name>`, `<email_id>`, `<App Description>` only where noted).

## When this applies

- After `bench new-app` (scaffold is not done until this setup is complete)
- When the user asks to set up / harden a custom app (lint, pre-commit, CI)
- When adding missing root tooling files under `apps/<app_name>/`

## Required sequence

1. Activate bench env: `source env/bin/activate` (from bench root)
2. Replace `apps/<app_name>/pyproject.toml` with the template in the guide
   - Customize only `[project]` (name, email, description, real dependencies)
   - Copy `[tool.black]` through `[tool.ruff.format]` **unchanged**
   - Do not list frappe in `dependencies` (bench manages it)
3. `pip install pre-commit` then `pre-commit install` inside the app directory
4. Create these files **verbatim** from the guide (substitute `<app_name>` in
   pre-commit prettier/eslint excludes):

   | File | Notes |
   | ---- | ----- |
   | `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | Includes local `check-max-lines` hook |
   | `scripts/check_max_lines.py` | Max 250 lines per Python file |
   | `.eslintrc` | Add missing globals to `globals` if lint fails |
   | `.flake8` | Copy as-is |
   | `commitlint.config.js` | Conventional commits |
   | `.editorconfig` | Tabs for py/js; spaces for json |
   | `.github/workflows/linters.yml` | See versions below |

5. Copy `project_base_template/commands/` into
   `apps/<app_name>/<app_name>/commands/` (`__init__.py`,
   `export_fixtures.py`, `README.md`) — see Section 4.7 of the guide
6. In `hooks.py`, add `custom_fixtures` and `commands` (see Section 4.7)
7. Verify final tree matches Section 6 of the guide

## CI workflow choice

Use **only one** `linters.yml`:

- **Version B (new projects)** — after pre-commit is configured: includes
  commit-lint, pre-commit action, semgrep, pip-audit
- **Version A (existing / no pre-commit in CI)** — commit-lint, semgrep,
  pip-audit only (no pre-commit job)

Prefer Version B for newly scaffolded apps.

## Expected app root

```
apps/<app_name>/
├── .github/workflows/linters.yml
├── <app_name>/
│   └── commands/          # from project_base_template/commands/
├── scripts/check_max_lines.py
├── .eslintrc
├── .flake8
├── .pre-commit-config.yaml
├── .editorconfig
├── commitlint.config.js
├── pyproject.toml
├── README.md
├── license.txt
└── .gitignore
```

## Agent checklist before finishing

- [ ] All files from the guide exist with correct content
- [ ] `<app_name>` placeholders replaced in pre-commit excludes
- [ ] `pyproject.toml` tool sections match the shared template
- [ ] `commands/` copied from `project_base_template/commands/`
- [ ] `hooks.py` has `custom_fixtures` and `commands` wired (Section 4.7)
- [ ] Correct `linters.yml` version chosen
- [ ] User told to run `pre-commit install` / `pre-commit run --all-files` if
      not already done in this session
